============================================================
PIPELINE ACCEPTANCE ADJUDICATION — SUMMARY AND VERDICT
============================================================
Date:           2026-08-14
Platform:       win32, sm_120 (RTX 5060), CUDA 13.3
Question:       Is the ORIGINAL unconstrained 47-register pipelined B-TMA
                (register_tiled_gemm_TMA_B_pipeline.cu) truly faster than the
                accepted production kernel, under a clean round-robin benchmark?

Prior state:    Original pipeline had been classified REJECT/NOISE under a
                grouped (non-interleaved) benchmark with a host-pre-test mismatch
                (production ran correctness; pipeline ran --timing-only).
                Those methodology flaws are fixed here.

============================================================
METHOD (fixed)
============================================================
A = accepted timing control (register_tiled_gemm_accepted_timing_control.cu):
    byte-identical kernel to production; host harness extended ONLY to add
    --timing-only. Resource-verified: 40 reg / 8192 B / 0 spills = production.
P = original pipeline, --timing-only.
Both invoked with --timing-only => identical host pre-test (warmup + 1 timed
launch), removing the earlier mismatch.
TRUE sample-level round-robin: 4 rounds x 30 A/P pairs; pair order alternates
(odd = A then P, even = P then A) to cancel order/drift bias.

============================================================
