Contamination: NONE in any round. GPU idle 2-7% util, P1, ~2.5 GHz, 52-54 C
per round; only benign Windows/DX processes present (see gpu_state log).

============================================================
ACCEPTANCE GATE
============================================================
1. 9/9 correctness remains PASS ........................ YES (established)
2. TMA overlap remains proven (UTMALDG, prefetch-before-compute) . YES
3. >=3 of 4 valid round medians show pipeline >1% faster: R2,R3,R4 -> 3/4 YES
4. Combined median improvement >1% ...................... -3.49%  YES
5. Median paired improvement >1% ........................ -3.30%  YES
6. Pipeline wins >=70% of valid pairs ................... 77.5%   YES
7. No single contaminated/outlier-heavy round carries it .. YES
   (rounds uncontaminated; the weakest round, R1, shows +0.18% by raw median but
    -2.35% paired median and 19/30 wins; excluding R1 leaves 74/90 = 82% wins and
    a clearly negative delta, so no single round drives the verdict)

=> ALL 7 GATES PASS.

============================================================
VERDICT: ACCEPT ORIGINAL PIPELINED B-TMA AS CANDIDATE
============================================================
The earlier REJECT/NOISE classification of the original 47-register pipelined
B-TMA is SUPERSEDED by this controlled round-robin acceptance evidence. Under a
clean A/P round-robin the pooled pipeline wins 93/120 pairs with a -3.3% median
paired delta and -3.49% combined-median delta vs the accepted kernel.

Caveats (stated per policy):
* Mechanism: WHY the 47-register pipeline is faster (compiler scheduling /
  instruction selection / ILP) is a HYPOTHESIS only; not isolated.
* identical max_rel values shown so far are TOLERANCE-level equivalence, NOT a
  proven bitwise (byte-identical) comparison; a bitwise check was not performed.
* One weak round (R1) had a positive raw-median delta (+0.18%) though its paired
  median and win count favored the pipeline; the aggregate over 120 pairs is
  decisive.
* Accepted control used --timing-only exactly like the pipeline, so host pre-test
  behavior was identical (the prior group-order + host-mismatch bias is removed).

Action: This is an ACCEPTED CANDIDATE, not a production promotion. Production
source is NOT modified. STOP for review before any promotion.

